From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winex11: a touch is a click; a program's drag of its frame ends

David 2026-10-03, on a ThinkPad X1's touchscreen: windows could not be
chosen or dragged with a touch, nor text selected (Firefox for Linux, which
handles touches itself, could); and GNOME Secrets' window stuck to the
pointer -- the resize arrows, then the window following the mouse however
often he clicked -- after a touch and the mouse together.

- Touch: winex11 asked XInput2 for touch events on its windows, so the X
  server gave them touches and no pointer; Wine made touches WM_POINTER
  messages only, which hardly a program handles, and does not turn them
  into the mouse's as Windows does. It no longer asks: the X server
  presses, moves and releases the pointer for a touch, and every program
  can be touched as it can be clicked. (Touch-aware programs lose
  WM_POINTER for touches.)
- A program drawing its own title bar asks the window manager to move or
  size it (_NET_WM_MOVERESIZE, 0803), and the frame ran Wine's move loop,
  which ends at the button's release. Started after the release (a tap, a
  quick click) or with the pointer still the program's, it waited for ever
  and the program got the clicks. Now it starts only with a button down,
  the pointer grabbed for the frame first (retried while the program lets
  go of it); Wine's capture keeps the grab and releases it as the loop ends.

Test: test/ownframe-gate.sh (a quick click on the program's title bar:
the frame does not follow the pointer after -- wine-sg 148 fails it;
mutant SG_MUTANT_MOVERESIZE_ANYWAY). The touch half needs a touchscreen
(the X1): Xvfb has none, and another client's XInput2 selection cannot be
read (mutant SG_MUTANT_TOUCH_AS_POINTER_MESSAGES restores the old one).
---
--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/mouse.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/mouse.c
@@ -273,12 +273,21 @@
         XISetMask( mask_bits, XI_RawMotion );
         XISetMask( mask_bits, XI_ButtonPress );
     }
+#ifdef SG_MUTANT_TOUCH_AS_POINTER_MESSAGES
     else
     {
         XISetMask( mask_bits, XI_TouchBegin );
         XISetMask( mask_bits, XI_TouchUpdate );
         XISetMask( mask_bits, XI_TouchEnd );
     }
+#endif
+    /* Stained Glass OS (David 2026-10-03: on the X1's touchscreen windows
+     * could not be chosen or dragged, nor text selected): asked for touch
+     * events, the X server gave Wine's windows touches and no pointer; Wine
+     * made them WM_POINTER messages only, which hardly a program handles,
+     * and does not turn them into the mouse's as Windows does. Not asked,
+     * the X server presses, moves and releases the pointer for a touch:
+     * every program can be touched as it can be clicked. */
 
     pXISelectEvents( display, window, &mask, 1 );
 }
--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/sg_embed.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/sg_embed.c
@@ -923,8 +923,43 @@
             X11DRV_expect_error( display, ignore_error, NULL );
             XDeleteProperty( display, event->xany.window, moveresize_atom( display ) );
             X11DRV_check_error();
-            if (dir == 8) NtUserPostMessage( hwnd, WM_SYSCOMMAND, SC_MOVE | HTCAPTION, 0 );
-            else if (dir >= 0 && dir < 8) NtUserPostMessage( hwnd, WM_SYSCOMMAND, SC_SIZE | size_edge[dir], 0 );
+            /* Stained Glass OS (David 2026-10-03: GNOME Secrets' window stuck
+             * to the pointer, clicks or not, after a touch): Wine's move loop
+             * ends at the button's release -- started after it (a tap, a quick
+             * click), or with the pointer still grabbed by the program, it
+             * waited for ever, the program getting the clicks. So: only with a
+             * button down, and with the pointer grabbed for the frame first
+             * (the program lets go of it as it asks; Wine's capture keeps it
+             * and lets it go when the loop ends). */
+            if (dir >= 0 && dir <= 8)
+            {
+                Window root_ret, child_ret, frame = 0;
+                int rx, ry, wx, wy, k, st = GrabNotViewable;
+                unsigned int mask = 0;
+                struct sg_embed *e;
+
+                pthread_mutex_lock( &embed_mutex );
+                if ((e = find_hwnd( hwnd ))) frame = e->frame;
+                pthread_mutex_unlock( &embed_mutex );
+                XQueryPointer( display, DefaultRootWindow( display ), &root_ret, &child_ret, &rx, &ry, &wx, &wy, &mask );
+#ifdef SG_MUTANT_MOVERESIZE_ANYWAY
+                mask |= Button1Mask;
+#endif
+                if (frame && (mask & (Button1Mask | Button2Mask | Button3Mask)))
+                {
+                    for (k = 0; k < 20; k++)
+                    {
+                        st = XGrabPointer( display, frame, False, ButtonPressMask | ButtonReleaseMask | PointerMotionMask,
+                                           GrabModeAsync, GrabModeAsync, None, None, CurrentTime );
+                        if (st == GrabSuccess) break;
+                        usleep( 10000 );
+                    }
+                    TRACE( "move/size %ld: pointer grab %d\n", dir, st );
+                    if (dir == 8) NtUserPostMessage( hwnd, WM_SYSCOMMAND, SC_MOVE | HTCAPTION, 0 );
+                    else NtUserPostMessage( hwnd, WM_SYSCOMMAND, SC_SIZE | size_edge[dir], 0 );
+                }
+                else TRACE( "move/size %ld asked with no button down: not started\n", dir );
+            }
         }
         break;
     case UnmapNotify:
